From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: date-time callback fields, MirrorIcon, shadow text, DelMRUString, page sizes, tab drops

- Date and time picker: the app-defined fields of a format ('X', 'XX',
  ...) were shown as "x" and ignored keys (FIXMEs). Their width is asked
  of the parent (DTN_FORMATQUERY), their text too (DTN_FORMAT, with the
  current date), and their keys go to it (DTN_WMKEYDOWN); a date the
  parent changes is taken and DTN_DATETIMECHANGE sent.
- MirrorIcon (a stub that failed) replaces the icons it is given by
  mirrored copies.
- DrawShadowText draws a real shadow: the text's shape, softened, in the
  shadow colour, blended at the offset asked for (it was a hard copy one
  pixel off whatever the offset).
- DelMRUString (a stub that said yes) removes the item at the position
  from the list and the registry, keeping the slots in order.
- PSM_RECALCPAGESIZES (a stub) sizes the sheet and its pages again for
  the pages it has now.
- A tooltip answers WM_NOTIFYFORMAT: Unicode for NF_QUERY, and with
  NF_REQUERY asks the window again and notifies its tools in its format.
- Tabs: TCIF_RTLREADING is kept and drawn right to left;
  TCS_EX_REGISTERDROP makes the control a drop target that asks its
  parent for the tab's own target (TCN_GETOBJECT) and hands it the drag.
  Wine's tab test no longer marks the style's read-back as todo.

Wine's comctl32 datetime, misc, mru, propsheet, tab and tooltips tests:
no failures (one tab todo now passes and is no longer marked).

Gate: test/ccmisc-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/ccmisc-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_FORMATQUERY (comctl32/datetime.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_MIRROR, SG_MUTANT_FLAT_SHADOW (comctl32/commctrl.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_RECALC (comctl32/propsheet.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_TAB_DROP
(comctl32/tab.c).
